  "description" : "The 2513 tolerance, which is the single most delicate rule on this screen. Both dates are 1500-01-01, which precedes the Lillian epoch CEEDAYS supports, so CSUTLDTC returns severity 0003 with CSUTLDTC-RESULT-MSG-NUM = '2513' - app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl:66 declares 88 FC-UNSUPP-RANGE VALUE X'000309D159C3C5C5', whose first halfword X'0003' is the severity and whose second X'09D1' is decimal 2513. The '0000' test at :397 therefore fails and control reaches :400, IF CSUTLDTC-RESULT-MSG-NUM NOT = '2513' - which is false, so the rejection is skipped and the screen proceeds exactly as if the date were valid. The second call site at :417-427 applies the identical rule to TPROCDTI. The run ends on the confirmation guard, proving both dates were accepted: turning this tolerance into a rejection would refuse dates the legacy program accepts, and dropping it would accept dates it refuses.",
